# Manifest of the gd test suites scripts/run-gd-tests.sh MUST find under
# council/tests/gd/. Line format (v2, shared with cad/tests/gd/EXPECTED_SUITES
# and pcb/tests/gd/EXPECTED_SUITES):
#
#     <filename> [assertions=N] [real-worker]
#
# A suite going missing (deleted, renamed, moved off the glob) or appearing
# unregistered is a loud, named pre-flight failure in both directions.
#
# The assertion count is pinned from a run that got through every section with
# the backend up. The executable pin below is the observed total; it includes
# the original sections plus the regression cases added at landing.
#
# A lower count means a setup guard fired rather than exercising its section.
#
# SETUP THIS SUITE NEEDS beyond the runner's own: section 6 drives the REAL
# backend over stdio, so council-plugin must be built first —
#     (cd council && go build -o council-plugin ./)
# and the Minerva checkout needs its `terminal` GDExtension built, like every
# other suite that starts a real plugin subprocess. Without the binary the
# section fails by name; it does not skip.

# The native panel end to end: mounted through the real PluginScenePanelHost
# from the real manifest, saved and reloaded byte-for-byte, round-tripped
# through a plugin_data note, an unreadable document preserved rather than
# replaced, the host envelope measured against the host's own cap, and two
# panels in two projects kept apart against one backend store; a document from
# an older schema migrated on open; a run saved in flight demoted on reopen and
# continued explicitly without re-asking the seat that answered; and a panel
# reopened onto a document the engine had already carried further, while a
# lagging copy opened alongside another panel is replaced rather than merged;
# and a round driven straight down the MCP tool door, with no panel in the
# exchange, reaching the panel that owns that document before it saves; and the
# one text derivation a session hands over, held to the fixture that is its
# oracle and proved to be the same text through both of its callers.
